      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Start the comment with saying that FILL_RETURN_BUFFER is not needed here, to make it immediately clear what this whole comment is about?\n\n2. IMHO no need to mention ADL/PTL and details like pkvm_relax_cpu_bugs, we can just say that pKVM requires eIBRS.\n\n3. The last sentence sounds a bit too verbose and not quite clear to me. \"it will execute the CALL instruction and let it retire before the first RET instruction\" - but this is true for the original code in vmx/vmenter.S as well, since it executes `call vmx_spec_ctrl_restore_host` before the unbalanced RET? And this CALL is not really enough to fix the issue for that original code, it needs at least CALL + INT3 (provided by X86_FEATURE_RSB_VMEXIT_LITE) for that? So this sentence seems misleading?\n\n4. Split into paragraphs for readability?\n\nMaybe just something like:\n\n```\n\t/* \n\t * Unlike in vmx/vmenter.S, no need for FILL_RETURN_BUFFER here.\n\t *\n\t * pKVM requires eIBRS which has its own protection against poisoned RSB,\n\t * so no need for RSB filling.\n\t *\n\t * If eIBRS is affected by PBRSB, still no need for RSB filling here,\n\t * since there is no unbalanced RET after host vmexit.\n\t */\n```\n\n?",
