      "message": "\u003eThe last sentence sounds a bit too verbose and not quite clear to me. \"it will execute the CALL instruction and let it retire before the first RET instruction\" - but this is true for the original code in vmx/vmenter.S as well, since it executes call vmx_spec_ctrl_restore_host before the unbalanced RET? And this CALL is not really enough to fix the issue for that original code, it needs at least CALL + INT3 (provided by X86_FEATURE_RSB_VMEXIT_LITE) for that? So this sentence seems misleading?\n\nMaybe saying it as \"it will execute the CALL instruction and let it retire before the balanced RET instruction\" is more clear. The vmx/vmenter.S executes `call vmx_spec_ctrl_restore_host` but the RET instruction in `vmx_spec_ctrl_restore_host` is unbalanced ret, thus it is not able to retire CALL instruction before the balanced RET instruction. Anyway, if this sentence misleading the reader, I am fine we just simplify it.",
